url: https://github.com/sayam/verifiable-gates
abstract: >-
  A registry of CI gates for software projects built with or without
  AI coding agents, and the rules behind them as an agent skill.
  Each of the 92 rules records the incident that produced it, so a
  reader can judge whether the conditions that produced it still
  hold; a rule with no incident is a preference, and preferences do
  not earn a gate. The bundle ships nine standalone checkers that
  decide part of the catalogue mechanically in a project that has
  installed nothing, an installer and a doctor that run them, and a
  renderer that turns the catalogue into rule sheets an AI coding
  agent can be handed; the other rules are written for an agent to
  read. A rule and its enforcement are kept in separate files
  because they have separate lifetimes. The reference implementation
  the rules were extracted from is held to every rule published
  here, and a test in that project checks both directions. The code
  is Apache-2.0; the rule catalogue and the documentation are CC BY
  4.0.
keywords:
  - software governance
  - AI-assisted development
  - continuous integration
  - secure software development
  - developer experience
